- op: discuss  # f004
  at: '2026-10-31T23:33:41Z'  # f004
  by: agent  # f004
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f004
  clock: 2  # f004
  nonce: f004  # f004
  message: "Fix on local branch jgstern-agent/fix/zakij, commit 424004303e (on top of the WI-zakij fix e26e5a942b; not pushed; integration pending). Premise reproduced: B.vue (<script lang=\"ts\"> + <script setup lang=\"ts\">) gave two typescript:B.vue:1-1:file:file Symbols (spans 1-3, 4-7); C.svelte (JS context=\"module\" + TS instance) gave a javascript: and a typescript: file node. Decision: the one file symbol is typescript when any block is TypeScript (superset; Vue's compiler rejects <script> and <script setup> of different langs), else javascript; its span covers all blocks; members keep their block's language but fold the file symbol's identity anchor (new _extract_symbols file_lang parameter). Edges: _extract_edges now starts imports/require edges at the module_symbol it is handed (identical id for every non-SFC caller), so a JS block's imports no longer hang off a javascript: file id with no symbol. One helper, _parse_sfc_blocks, now serves the main loop (one loop over both hosts) and the single-file _analyze_svelte_file / _analyze_vue_file (one _analyze_sfc_file, which also resolves across blocks now). Tests: test_js_ts_sfc_one_file_symbol.py (8 cases; 7 RED on pre-fix code; edge-anchor-only mutant fails the 2 mixed-language cases). Affected-test run: 12054 passed, 16 xfailed, changed files 100% covered. Corpus A/B (129 components in 5 dirs that hold the construct): file symbols 132 -> 129, duplicate ids 2 -> 0. Not changed, a cross-analyzer question for whoever owns it: lang-common svelte.py / vue.py / astro.py anchor their template edges on a svelte:/vue:/astro: file id, beside this analyzer's typescript:/javascript: file symbol for the same path (on the scratch fixture, whose templates use no components, survey showed only the one typescript: file node per component)."  # f004
